Z||000005||ezsurf||08-25-99||10:31 PM||||Stetz, what kind of engine do you have?<p>Wisconsin, in order to set the timing the ALCL (assembly line communication link) must be grounded. This puts the computer in the field test mode. Remove the cover plate where the cancer ignition device is. The connector plug is behind this plate.  If you are looking directly at the plug you will see two terminals in the lower left hand corner. Jump a wire between these terminals.  This will put the computer in the field test mode so you can proprerly set the timing.
Z||000006||FieroSTETZ||08-25-99||10:54 PM||||thanks for the response! how do i find the thingamajiggy that i need to jumper? in my non car related escapades, i am a computer nerd (my job) so i am familiar with jumpering, but just where would i find this "doodad"? i have the newer version of the chilton's fiero manual, if someone could maybe tell me the page number for this procedure or something, that would be GREAT! thanks so much, and I'll tell you all how it turns out... Thanks much, and may the Fiero live on!
Z||000007||batboy||08-25-99||11:57 PM||||The ECM on a Fiero is behind the little plate where the cigarette lighter is mounted (EZ's cancer ignition device).
Z||000008||ezsurf||08-26-99||12:13 AM||||Stetz,<br>You can use a paper clip, but any <br>ordinary piece of wire will do.  <br>Allegator clips won't help, <br>because you can't get them to <br>contact the terminals. If you are <br>setting the timng by yourself, <br>make sure the wire stays connected <br>while you set the timing. If your <br>wire won't stay connected, then <br>someone has to hold the wire and <br>someone has to set the timing.
Z||000009||FieroSTETZ||08-26-99||05:50 PM||||Okay, I tried adjusting the problem, and the timing mark shows my timing as being correct, but i still have the same problems as before i.e. lumpy, constant backfiring (BTW, mine is an 86 SE 2m6, 4spd man.) i AM getting error codes when i jumper the thing, but i don't know what they are. it is like this .-..- and then repeats... also, when i jumper it then start, the check engine blinks steadily instead of the afore mentioned pattern. if anyone has any further ideas, let me know please! i need my baby back!
Z||000010||ezsurf||08-26-99||07:26 PM||||Stetz,<br>You have the same car as I do. So I should be able to help.  It would help to know how long have you had the car. Did you just buy it?  Also, have you just done any recent engine work?  When did the car start doing this? <br> You do not have to start the car to get the computer codes.  Just turn the ignition switch to run and attach the jumper wire.  The computer flashes each code three times, then it goes to the next code.  After it goes through all the codes, it repeats them.  There are web sites that give a breakdown on what the codes mean, I'll find one and post it.  Give me some more info, and I'll see if I can help.
Z||000011||ezsurf||08-26-99||07:38 PM||||Stetz,<br>Check out this site http://thefieroclub.com/osg/fiero_osg/osg.html
Z||000012||JetroGT||08-26-99||08:32 PM||||When you reinstalled the injectors, did you wire up the injector harness correctly? A loose or disconected vacume hose? A bad TPS "throttle position sensor." O2 sensor? Thats all I can think of that would make it run lumpy.
Z||000013||FieroSTETZ||08-26-99||11:45 PM||||I live in oceanside, CA, and was wondering if there is anyone who could help me out with my car. Don't get me mistaken, i love my fiero, but I am at my wits end with this car. i bought it nearly a month ago (my first car purchase, i talked them down almost a thousand dollars!!!) and it ran "okay" (okay being the fact that the previous owner had installed an intake manifold gasket improperly, so 2 cylinders did not run at idle... all the problems started after installing all new gaskets from a gasket set i paid like 120 bucks for at Autozone.) Now, it won't run for more than 2 minutes before dying, its incredibly lumpy, and i am so frustrated i accidentally called my fiero (named hot sh*t by my girlfriend) a piece of crap. if there is anyone in my area, please let me know and perhaps i could work out a deal. if necessary, i could pay SOME money (i don't have much) but i would give what i can just to have my baby back!
