Z||000015||Cliff Pennock||08-27-99||03:34 AM||||Ok, perhaps a stupid question but: did you connect the spark plug wires the right way? Sounds like the firing order is wrong.<p>The only reason an engine backfires (when the timing is correct) is when a cylinder gets fuel, but no spark. I would check the following:<p>1) Check if plug wires are connected properly (I think the Chilton manual lists the firing order incorrectly)<br>2) Check for broken plug wires<br>3) Remove tachfilter and see how engine runs<br>4) Check plugs<br>5) Replace ignition module<p>Hope this helps.
Z||000016||FieroSTETZ||08-27-99||11:42 AM||||the chilton manual lists the firing order wrong? geez! that might be it, i used the chilton's manual to reinstall all the plug wires! also, i came to a realization last night, i forogot to fully disconnect the battery until well into the project, could this have made my computer barf? thanks cliff for the recommendation, im gonna see if the online service manual has the proper plug settings.
