Z||000022||FieroSTETZ||08-28-99||10:54 PM||||the beast lives again! thanks for all the help people. it turns out i had a worn lifter (i used a really old popular mechanics engine diagnostics tip booklet i found in my garage) adjusting the lifter allowed me to get the car to turn over, with compression on ALL cylinders... im so happy, i have to go buy a new set of intake manifold gaskets, but mechanically, the car is fine. the only problems i can forsee are any that the computer might have. once again, thanks so much for the help everyone, you all are great. anyone needs any help with anything, let me know, i owe you all!
